```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Frontend"
        A[Next.js Web App] --> B[Mapbox/Leaflet Map]
        A --> C[Shadcn/UI Components]
    end

    subgraph "Backend"
        D[Node.js / FastAPI] --> E[PostGIS Database]
        D --> F[Redis Cache]
        D --> G[Elasticsearch]
    end

    subgraph "Blockchain Layer"
        H[Polygon Network] --> I[Land NFT Contract]
        H --> J[Registry Contract]
        H --> K[Dispute Resolution Contract]
    end

    subgraph "ML Pipeline"
        L[Satellite Imagery] --> M[SAM / YOLO]
        M --> N[Boundary Detection]
        N --> O[Encroachment Alerts]
    end

    subgraph "Decentralized Storage"
        P[IPFS / Filecoin] --> Q[Land Documents]
        P --> R[Survey Maps]
    end

    A --> D
    D --> H
    D --> P
    D --> L
```

---

## 🎯 What Makes This Unique (Hackathon Winning Points)

1. **1.1 cm precision** — No other land registry system operates at this granularity
2. **NFT-based ownership** — Each land parcel is a verifiable on-chain asset
3. **AI-powered dispute prevention** — Catch encroachments before they become court cases
4. **Real-world impact** — Directly addresses a problem affecting 600M+ Indians
5. **Government-ready** — Designed to work WITH existing systems (ULPIN, DigiLocker, Aadhaar)

---

## 📋 Hackathon MVP Scope

For a hackathon demo, focus on:

1. ✅ Map interface where user can draw a polygon to define a land parcel
2. ✅ Convert the polygon to GeoHash-12 cells and display them
3. ✅ Mint the parcel as an NFT on a local/test blockchain (Hardhat)
4. ✅ Store metadata in PostgreSQL + PostGIS
5. ✅ Show ownership history and transfer flow
6. ✅ Basic satellite image overlay showing registered vs. actual boundaries
7. ✅ Government dashboard to approve/reject registrations

> [!TIP]
> For the hackathon, use **Polygon Mumbai testnet** (free, fast) and **Mapbox free tier** (50K map loads/month). Both require no upfront cost.
